    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: unify `customerCode` + `membershipNumber` into `memberId`\n\nThe new `memberId` is formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (e.g. `NSW2716E6609E1`):\n- **REGION** \u2014 region code from postcode (`Locality.regionOf`)\n- **FY** \u2014 2-digit fiscal year of the registrationDate (`FiscalYear.shortYear`)\n- **HASH8** \u2014 the existing SHA-256-over-(telephone+lastName) first-8-upper-hex identity (`Hash8`)\n- **CHK** \u2014 a single Luhn digit over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`\n\n### What changed\n- **`model/MemberId.java`** (new) \u2014 the one place the id is composed from its segments.\n- **`model/CheckDigit.java`, `model/MembershipNumber.java`** \u2014 deleted (their logic now lives in the CHK and FY segments of `memberId`).\n- **`Owner.java`** + all four DB `schema.sql` files \u2014 `customerCode`/`customer_code` renamed to `memberId`/`member_id` (widened to `VARCHAR(32)` to fit the longer format plus collision suffix).\n- **`AssignCustomerCode` \u2192 `AssignMemberId`** \u2014 computes the base id and keeps the same `-<n>` collision handling, now against existing `memberId`s. Wired into `owners.POST.yml` (step renamed `assignMemberId`).\n- **`Locality.of(Owner)`** \u2014 reads the REGION segment as the leading letters of `memberId` (the format has no dash separator now), with the same postcode/city fallback. This is how `OwnerSegment` references the memberId.\n- **`FiscalYear.of(Owner)`** \u2014 reads the FY segment back out of `memberId` when present, falling back to registrationDate \u2014 so the fiscal-year value references the memberId.\n- **`AuditOwnerCreated` + `OwnerCreatedEvent`** \u2014 audit line and JSON event now carry `memberId` instead of `customerCode`/`membershipNumber`.\n- **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 dropped the `checkDigit` and `membershipNumber` mappings; `memberId` auto-maps by name.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 removed the three old field schemas, added `memberId`, and updated the `locality` description.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreReturnsUnifiedMemberId` passes (memberId starts with `NSW`, contains the HASH8, and `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` are gone), and `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nWant me to save a memory note about this identity subsystem, or is this good as-is?",
